{
  "email": "dana.whitfield@brightline.example",
  "reason": "Ticket sender requests install of a free PDF editor from an external link; need department and title for software request approval per KB-027."
}

{
  "outcome": "resolved",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Dana, I can't install that PDF editor from the link in the email. Software that arrives by email link hasn't been security-reviewed, so we don't install it directly. Please first check the Company Portal (Software Center) on your laptop, since approved PDF editors may already be listed there and you can install them yourself. If the tool isn't there, the request needs approval from your manager and a security review of the app. Once that's done, the help desk can help with the install. Please don't open or run the setup file from that link in the meantime.",
  "internal_note": "Ticket from Dana Whitfield (CEO, VIP, user_id 1, device BL-LT-0101). Request: install free PDF editor from external link http://free-pdf-tools.example/setup.exe, which came from a vendor email. Account is active, not blocked, no failed logins. Per KB-027, do not install software from an emailed link; direct user to Company Portal first; otherwise it needs manager approval and security review. No install action taken. Triage marked possible_social_engineering false. The link came from a vendor and the domain is unvetted, so the technician may want to confirm with security whether the vendor email is legitimate, and whether the domain should be checked, though no sign of compromise was seen. No escalation made because the manager approval step has not yet happened; re-escalate to Tier 2 with app name, version, business reason and approver once approved and not in Company Portal.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-027"
  ],
  "confidence": "high"
}
